e the comma, read the 'Amount in Words' printed on the bill (e.g. 'FOUR THOUSAND FOUR HUNDRED AND NINETY RUPEES ONLY') to confirm the thousands digit.\n- Extract all numeric fields (quantity, unit_rate, total_amount, subtotal, cgst, sgst, igst, declared_total) as strings.\n\nExtract the invoice details into JSON matching this schema:\n- vendor_name: (string)\n- gstin: (string or null)\n- invoice_number: (string or null)\n- date: (string or null)\n- items: list of {description, quantity, unit_rate, total_amount} (numbers formatted as strings, e.g. \"2,535.00\")\n- subtotal: (string or null)\n- cgst: (string or null)\n- sgst: (string or null)\n- igst: (string or null)\n- declared_total: (string or null)\n\"\"\"\n\n    # First attempt: direct REST caller supporting both AQ. Bearer tokens and AIzaSy keys\n    try:\n        raw_text = await call_gemini_rest(api_key, mime_type, contents, prompt)\n        parsed = json.loads(raw_text)\n        cleaned = sanitize_and_clean_invoice(parsed)\n\n        # If declared_total is suspiciously smaller than subtotal or equals 774, reject the OCR hallucination:\n        subtot = float(cleaned.get(\"subtotal\", 0) or 0.0)\n        dec_tot = float(cleaned.get(\"declared_total\") if cleaned.get(\"declared_total\") is not None else (cleaned.get(\"total_declared\") or 0.0))\n        cgst = float(cleaned.get(\"cgst\", 0) or 0.0)\n        sgst = float(cleaned.get(\"sgst\", 0) or 0.0)\n        igst = float(cleaned.get(\"igst\", 0) or 0.0)\n        if (subtot > 0 and dec_tot < (subtot * 0.5)) or dec_tot in [774, 774.0]:\n            fallback_total = round(subtot + cgst + sgst + igst, 2)\n            cleaned[\"declared_total\"] = fallback_total\n            cleaned[\"total_declared\"] = fallback_total\n\n        return Response(content=json.dumps(cleaned), media_type=\"application/json\")\n    except Exception as rest_err:\n        print(f\"[AUDIT IT] Gemini REST attempt error: {rest_err}\")\n\n        # Secondary fallback using google.genai Cl