{"step_index":1585,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T19:48:33Z","input_tokens":2117,"cache_read_tokens":90352,"output_tokens":1518,"thinking":"The code snippet focuses on extracting CGST (Central Goods and Services Tax) values from invoice text. It uses a regular expression to identify lines containing \"CGST\" while excluding lines with \"subtotal\" or \"total in words\". The regular expression looks for currency amounts (₹ or numbers) in the Indian currency format. If found, these are parsed to extract the numerical values and store them as CGST values.\n\n\nFocus is shifting to the user-provided regular expressions for CGST, SGST, and IGST extraction, which explicitly define patterns for both tax rates and amounts. These patterns are designed to prevent accidental extraction of item quantities as taxes by requiring specific tax line formats. The regex structure uses two capture groups: an optional tax rate and a required currency amount. The presence of a value in the second group indicates a valid tax amount for extraction.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"python3 -c '\nimport re\n\ncgst_pat = re.compile(r\"(?:CGST|Central GST)[\\s@%]*([0-9\\.]+)?%?[\\s:]*[₹\\s]*([0-9,]+(?:\\.[0-9]{2})?)\", re.I)\n\nfor text in [\n    \"CGST @ 9%: 990.00\",\n    \"CGST 9%: 990.00\",\n    \"CGST @ 9% 990.00\",\n    \"Central GST 9.0% : ₹990.00\",\n    \"CGST: 990.00\",\n    \"CGST 990.00\",\n    \"20W LED Bulb 20 PCS\",\n    \"CGST @ 9%: 1,624.95\"\n]:\n    m = cgst_pat.search(text)\n    if m:\n        print(f\"MATCH: {text!r:30} -> g1={m.group(1)!r:10} g2={m.group(2)!r:10}\")\n    else:\n        print(f\"NO MATCH: {text!r}\")\n'","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolSummary":"Test CGST regex pattern"}}]}
